<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Sorrows of Young Werther</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1774">1774</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sorrows of Young Werther is an epistolary novel by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-wolfgang-von-goethe">Johann Wolfgang von Goethe</a>, published in 1774, about a young man's hopeless love for a woman engaged to another, ending in his suicide. It drew on Goethe's stay in Wetzlar in 1772, caused a sensation across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and is a key work of the Sturm und Drang movement.</p></div>
